                <pb facs="0619" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.6156 T 61/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-12T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>79. Department’s telegram number 52, August 10, 3 p.m. As the Government of
                    Panama has already expressed its disagreement with the views of the Department
                    relative to railroad construction (see despatch No. 1413, May 14), I am
                    withholding action upon paragraph 2 pending further instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">South</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
